From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 09:25:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(control): no release we send ghostty may open a link
 (KD-27)

libghostty now highlights a link on a plain hover rather than only under
ctrl, which is what KD-27 asked for. That makes `Surface.mouse.over_link`
true far more often, and ghostty opens a link on the *release* of a click
over one (`processLinks`).

Every release that reaches ghostty from a pane is either synthesised by
`_releaseMouseIfHeld` - already suppressed for exactly this reason, since
WT reports no release outside VT mouse mode - or sent from
`SendMouseEvent` while an application owns the mouse. Neither is a user's
link click: Windows Terminal answers that itself, on the press, and
`ControlInteractivity::PointerPressed` takes a ctrl+click over a link from
`GetHyperlink` and returns without forwarding it. So the second one is
suppressed too.

Insurance rather than a fix for an observed bug. ghostty stops refreshing
links once mouse reporting is on, but the `over_link` it last settled on
outlives that and is what `processLinks` tests.

Also corrects a comment in GhosttySettingsTranslator that still described
the highlight as happening under ctrl.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qm2sT9zLC2AndHGSanf2ws
---
 .../TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp         | 14 ++++++++++++++
 .../TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp  |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
index fcb89f8a0..038f1941a 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
@@ -1336,7 +1336,21 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
         case WM_LBUTTONUP:
         case WM_RBUTTONUP:
         case WM_MBUTTONUP:
+            // Suppressed for the same reason _releaseMouseIfHeld suppresses:
+            // ghostty opens a link on the release of a click over one, and no
+            // release that reaches it is ever a link click. WT answers that
+            // itself, on the *press* - a ctrl+click over a link never gets
+            // this far, since ControlInteractivity::PointerPressed takes it
+            // from GetHyperlink and returns.
+            //
+            // Insurance rather than a fix for an observed bug: an application
+            // owns the mouse on this path, so ghostty stops refreshing links,
+            // but the over_link it last settled on outlives that and is what
+            // processLinks tests. Now that a link highlights on a plain hover
+            // that state is reached far more often than it was.
+            _suppressOpenUrl = true;
             ghostty_surface_mouse_button(_surface, GHOSTTY_MOUSE_RELEASE, button, mods);
+            _suppressOpenUrl = false;
             _mouseDown = false;
             break;
 
diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp
index cbba18e9f..6f14b3507 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttySettingsTranslator.cpp
@@ -116,7 +116,7 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
 
         // WT's own switch for turning URL detection off, which ghostty spells
         // `link-url`. Both default to on, and both mean the same thing: with it
-        // off a URL in output is plain text - no highlight under ctrl, nothing
+        // off a URL in output is plain text - no highlight on hover, nothing
         // for ctrl+click to open. OSC 8 hyperlinks are unaffected either side;
         // an application that marks its own links keeps them.
         set("link-url", settings.DetectURLs() ? "true" : "false");
